<article class="env-lemma" id="0G45">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0G45">Lemma <span data-tag="0G45">29.34.2</span>.</a> Let $a : X \to S$ and $b : Y \to S$ be morphisms of schemes. Let $\mathcal{F}$ and $\mathcal{F}'$ be quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-modules. Let $D : \mathcal{F} \to \mathcal{F}'$ be a differential operator of order $k$ on $X/S$. Let $\mathcal{G}$ be a quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ Y$-module. Then there is a unique differential operator </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  D' : \text{pr}_1^*\mathcal{F} \otimes _{\mathcal{O}_{X \times _ S Y}} \text{pr}_2^*\mathcal{G} \longrightarrow \text{pr}_1^*\mathcal{F}' \otimes _{\mathcal{O}_{X \times _ S Y}} \text{pr}_2^*\mathcal{G}  \]
</div>
  <p> of order $k$ on $X \times _ S Y / Y$ such that $ D'(s \otimes t) = D(s) \otimes t $ for local sections $s$ of $\mathcal{F}$ and $t$ of $\mathcal{G}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      In case $X$, $Y$, and $S$ are affine, this follows, via Lemma <a href="/tag/0G44" data-tag="0G44">29.34.1</a>, from the corresponding algebra result, see Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0G37" data-tag="0G37">10.133.13</a>. In general, one uses coverings by affines (for example as in Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/01JS" data-tag="01JS">26.17.4</a>) to construct $D'$ globally. Details omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>